{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487376-how-would-a-vampire-have-consumption","id":1487376,"title":"How would a vampire have Consumption?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-21T06:12:01-07:00","id":1487376,"title":"How would a vampire have Consumption?","content":"I'd like to tell a storyline with a tragically doomed character in it so I need something that will kill a vampire slowly but surely, the way 'consumption' was viewed as a disease before modern medicine came into the action.<br /> <br /> Ideally it needs to be something that cannot be 'cured' so no curses and something that is suitably tragic and long-winded. Think of the way consumption is used in historical dramas - La Boheme, Val Kilmer in Tombstone, Nicole Kidman in Moulin Rouge, etc.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking somethign like silver/substance poisoning (is that even a thing?), some sort of degenerative flaw in the embrace, or ???<br /> <br /> Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T07:38:44-07:00","id":1487379,"title":"","content":"There is little in the way of diseases or poisons that can affect kindred, with the notable exception of magically created diseases like the Blood Curse (despite the name, not exactly a curse) that ravaged Atlanta and Berlin. Cainites of all factions are incredibly paranoid about those, and would probably destroy / blood hunt a potential vector if they suspect anything.<br /> <br /> The classic struggle for vampires is against their Beast, so maybe there is something there. Their Beast could be of a more devious kind that gets stronger the more they feed, and the 'Consumption' could be the reflection of growing hunger versus not feeding (which is definitely doomed to fail).<br /> <br /> Or maybe an especially unfortunate prey exclusion: they can only feed from blood that also hurts them- people with True Faith, or touched by Helios.<br /> <br /> Maybe they consumed the soul of something really strong which now destroys them from the inside (think Saulot vs Tremere).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T21:20:37-07:00","id":1487444,"title":"","content":"Chagas disease.<br /> <br /> It is caused by a blood-feeding parasitic protozoa, and despite being blood-borne it is unlikely to be transmitted from the vampire to others because of its extremely specific cycle. Even the vector, the kissing bug, do not infect with a bite, but with poop. Unless the sick vampire starts to poop on their victims, not going to affect anyone but them.<br /> <br /> You can take a look at pages about the disease from the CDC and others, and read about the Trypanosoma cruzi parasite. A weird mutation of a particular batch of parasites could have been able to become Ghouls inside the vampire. From then on, they have a very rare infection with an inner population of parasites that don't die and can literally consume them slowly but non-stop. Whatever happens in a normal human does not happen in a dead body, so the parasites just feed in blood cells and go on.<br /> <br /> Those buggers are terrible when they take hold. Anti-parasitic medicine can't get them all from your body if the infection goes on long enough, not even dialysis can solve it, you'll simply live the rest of your life with them. A vampire has less ways to notice the infection soon enough and no metabolism or bodily functions that can help against it or even process medicine. The same Blood intake the vampire needs will supply them with food.<br /> <br /> From this you can have fun with them either causing weird damage in several parts of the vampire's body in their search for blood, or just increasing Blood consumption because they're basically compulsory ghouls. One way or another, the symptoms may take the form of an apparent consumption in the vampire (while in humans it may damage the heart or the bowels, more rarely the liver) and be as identifiable and yet impossible to treat as tuberculosis in the 19th century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T02:52:43-07:00","id":1487466,"title":"","content":"Ok, ghouled blood parasites are a brilliant idea and I'm going to steal that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pu